WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:06.400
Hello, and welcome back to CZsWorld.

00:00:06.620 --> 00:00:07.980
Today we’re gonna be talking about the new
pre-roll ad for the Nun.

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:09.040
But you might want to turn your volume down
because *SCREAM*.

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:14.940
OK, I’m sorry.

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:15.780
I’m sorry.

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:16.780
I had to.

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:21.120
People are losing their minds right now over
this YouTube pre-roll ad for The Nun.

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:24.720
I assume you’ve probably seen it if you’re
watching this video, but if not, it looks

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:28.520
like this.

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:35.380
And this was brought to my attention by a
tweet going viral right now by a user named

00:00:35.390 --> 00:00:36.980
apple, who says:

00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:37.980
WARNING!

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:41.690
If you see an ad on youtube with the volume
sign being turned down and nothing else, ITS

00:00:41.690 --> 00:00:44.430
A JUMPSCARE for the new NUN movie coming out.

00:00:44.430 --> 00:00:48.870
i advise you look away and/or turn down the
volume if you have anxiety or just straight

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:52.140
up dislike jumpscares, pls rt to save a life

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:56.580
And that tweet has amassed over 100,000 retweets
in just 24 hours.

00:00:56.580 --> 00:01:00.470
There are articles being written about this
and people are actually calling for YouTube

00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:01.760
to take down the ad.

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:05.810
To which I have to say -- apple and whoever
else is tweeting about this right now.

00:01:05.810 --> 00:01:10.250
Why you gotta go and ruin the fun for everyone,
like me, who hasn’t seen the ad yet and

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:11.890
would have enjoyed that little scare.

00:01:11.890 --> 00:01:15.450
I mean people are acting like this is something
like the public needs to be aware of.

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:18.140
It’s not like the Nun comes out of your
screen and punches you in the face.

00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:20.560
It’s a loud noise, not a safety hazard.

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:23.060
And don’t you dare call for this ad to be
taken down.

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:26.840
We just got through the Adpocalypse, and it’s
hard enough for horror creators, like myself,

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:31.549
to earn a living because many brands no longer
consider horror content to be “safe” to

00:01:31.549 --> 00:01:32.549
advertise on.

00:01:32.549 --> 00:01:35.520
So now we finally have an ad that is tailor
made, to run in front of horror channels,

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:38.750
and you are not going to take that away from
us, just so that you don’t get startled

00:01:38.750 --> 00:01:39.829
for two seconds.

00:01:39.829 --> 00:01:43.579
Not to mention, that as long as you have ad
personalization on in your Google settings,

00:01:43.579 --> 00:01:44.579
which…

00:01:44.579 --> 00:01:47.240
I mean why would you not, I mean if you have
to see ads, you might as well see ones that

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:50.499
are relevant to your interests, but if you
have this on, and you don’t like horror

00:01:50.499 --> 00:01:52.810
movies, you probably won’t see the ad anyways.

00:01:52.810 --> 00:01:56.240
My ads are personalized to include horror
and I still haven’t seen this come up.

00:01:56.240 --> 00:02:00.119
And to be honest, as much as I love the concept
of this ad, and it reminds me of the classic

00:02:00.119 --> 00:02:04.440
YouTube screamer videos from the mid 2000s
that you never really see anymore… this

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:06.420
one’s not really fooling anybody.

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:09.649
First of all, it uses the Mac OS volume icon.

00:02:09.649 --> 00:02:12.660
And I don’t know, maybe there’s a different
version of the ad for Android or Windows,

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:16.569
but unless you’re on Mac, and you’re browsing
full screen so that the icon is actually centered

00:02:16.569 --> 00:02:19.930
on screen, you’re probably not going to
fall for it.

00:02:19.930 --> 00:02:21.620
But look at some of these responses.

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:26.959
“they need to display a warning before such
ads!!!! i cannot stand watching or even listening

00:02:26.959 --> 00:02:31.879
to anything related to the horror genre, my
heart’s too fragile to take it and my mind

00:02:31.879 --> 00:02:35.769
effs up bad &amp; it ends up haunting me for the
rest of my life!!!!”

00:02:35.769 --> 00:02:39.180
Well no, if you put a warning, that completely
ruins it.

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:41.970
The point of the ad is to catch you off guard
to get your attention.

00:02:41.970 --> 00:02:43.120
It’s marketing 101.

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:46.530
“I WATCHED IT MUTED AND IM STILL ON THE
VERGE OF TEARS”.

00:02:46.530 --> 00:02:51.180
Are we really that soft now that people are
in tears over a 6 second advert?

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:55.650
I mean, I’m so sick of everything being
watered down for my spineless excuse of a

00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:56.650
generation.

00:02:56.650 --> 00:02:59.719
Everything is constantly complained about
to the point that those of us with common

00:02:59.719 --> 00:03:04.810
sense can’t have nice things when Therese
here cannot handle the sight of a fictional

00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:05.810
character.

00:03:05.810 --> 00:03:09.099
“Great, I am already having anxiety from
knowing this exists.

00:03:09.099 --> 00:03:11.849
@YouTube would you please revise this add?

00:03:11.849 --> 00:03:14.390
It really isn't costumer friendly”

00:03:14.390 --> 00:03:16.859
Well actually, the Nun costume is very well
done.

00:03:16.859 --> 00:03:19.040
In my opinion the costumers did a great job.

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:22.590
But if you feel like this ad is giving you
too much anxiety, I’d recommend you crawl

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:25.471
back into the womb from which you came from
which you came from, because you’re not

00:03:25.471 --> 00:03:27.590
quite ready for the real world yet.

00:03:27.590 --> 00:03:32.060
“I won't be watching YouTube videos for
a while then , I hate jumpscares”

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:35.739
This is interesting because usually when someone
says they hate jumpscares, it’s because

00:03:35.739 --> 00:03:39.370
a movie relies on jumpscares too much and
doesn’t build that suspense that you need

00:03:39.370 --> 00:03:41.480
for a jumpscare to have a good payoff.

00:03:41.480 --> 00:03:45.440
Personally I really like jumpscares when they’re
done well, and in the context of this ad,

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:49.659
it uses the volume icon to throw off the viewer,
so if the prerequisites of being on a Mac

00:03:49.659 --> 00:03:52.349
and being full screen are met, I think it’s
a clever advert.

00:03:52.349 --> 00:03:56.829
But, it is a bit random theming wise… like
what do computers have to do with a Romanian

00:03:56.829 --> 00:03:57.829
Nun Demon?

00:03:57.829 --> 00:04:01.840
It would have actually fit better for a horror
movie about technology like Unfriended or

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:03.709
Friend Request… or…

00:04:03.709 --> 00:04:04.709
Scary...

00:04:04.709 --> 00:04:05.709
Friend...

00:04:05.709 --> 00:04:06.709
Internet...

00:04:06.709 --> 00:04:08.420
Movie……...?

00:04:08.420 --> 00:04:12.060
And it looks like before I even had the chance
to finish up this video and post it, YouTube

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:14.269
has already gone ahead and taken down the
ad.

00:04:14.269 --> 00:04:17.959
And they do point to this article on their
ad policy where they do have rules against

00:04:17.959 --> 00:04:20.209
violent and shocking ads in content.

00:04:20.209 --> 00:04:22.800
Including promotions that are likely to shock
or scare.

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:25.750
But then they say what they consider to be
shocking factors in ads are.

00:04:25.750 --> 00:04:29.020
Whether the video shows scenes containing
violent and/or graphic imagery that can be

00:04:29.020 --> 00:04:32.230
shocking or disturbing to viewers
Whether the video shows the graphic aftermath

00:04:32.230 --> 00:04:34.831
of a violent act
Whether the shots of violence or gore are

00:04:34.831 --> 00:04:37.660
the focal point of the scene in the video
And whether the violence contained in the

00:04:37.660 --> 00:04:40.140
video is realistic when posted in a dramatic
context

00:04:40.140 --> 00:04:43.540
And they also go on to say that other factors
include the camera angle and focus, and the

00:04:43.540 --> 00:04:44.710
clarity of the images in the video

00:04:44.710 --> 00:04:48.560
So it looks like this Nun ad doesn't technically
have of these factors that they consider to

00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:49.560
be shocking.

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:51.021
But I'm sure we'll never hear a statement
on it.

00:04:51.021 --> 00:04:53.521
And my advertiser revenue will go down as
a result of this.

00:04:53.521 --> 00:04:57.790
So this is the perfect opportunity to say
to check out my merch store and maybe pick

00:04:57.790 --> 00:05:00.160
up an item or two to support the channel.

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:04.931
But if you are one of those people whose life
was not ruined by this ad, then drop me a

00:05:04.931 --> 00:05:05.931
like on this video.

00:05:05.931 --> 00:05:09.840
I’m genuinely curious to see what the like
to dislike ratio comes out to on this one.

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:14.490
And remember to subscribe to CZsWorld for
more great horror content every week, ring

00:05:14.490 --> 00:05:17.130
that deathbell for notifications… you know
what?

00:05:17.130 --> 00:05:21.730
Ring that thing loud enough to startle some
complainer on the internet, and I’ll see

00:05:21.730 --> 00:05:23.270
you in the next one.

00:05:23.270 --> 00:05:25.200
Assuming we both survive.

